# Orchestrate: Cursor as manager, Codex and Claude Code CLIs as parallel workers

Check `HANDOFF.md` "In flight" and open `grok/*` PRs first so local workers don't collide with
cloud agents Grok started. Update `HANDOFF.md` (In flight, Open work) when you merge.

Scripts live in `scripts/orchestrate/`. State lives in `.ai/` and `.worktrees/` (both gitignored).

## Phase 1 — Architecture & contracts (no application code)
1. Break the feature into 2–4 tasks that touch **disjoint files**. If two tasks must share an interface, write it first in `.ai/contracts.md` (and commit any shared stub/interface code to the base branch so workers branch from it).
2. Write `.ai/task-<name>.md` per task. First line is a `# Title` (used as the commit message). Include: goal, exact files to create/modify, files NOT to touch, contract references, acceptance criteria, tests to add, and the verify command (`scripts/test.sh <paths>`).
3. Show the specs to the user and wait for approval.

## Phase 2 — Dispatch
1. Base branch must be clean (`git status`); commit contracts/stubs first.
2. Run in the background: `MAX_PARALLEL=3 scripts/orchestrate/dispatch.sh <name> <name>:claude ...`
   Codex is the default worker (OS sandbox, no network). Append `:claude` for Claude Code (tool
   allowlist, git and network denied), which suits larger refactors and docs. Mixing both in one
   wave also spreads rate limits across two providers.
3. Poll with `scripts/orchestrate/status.sh` (use `TAIL=20` for more log). Do not edit files inside `.worktrees/` while workers run.

## Phase 3 — Merge, integrate, QA
1. Read `.ai/logs/<name>.exit`, `.ai/handoff-<name>.md`, and `git diff HEAD...agent/<name>` for each task. Reject or fix work that strays outside its spec.
2. `git merge --no-ff agent/<name>` one branch at a time; resolve conflicts; run `scripts/test.sh` after each merge.
3. `scripts/orchestrate/cleanup.sh --delete-branches`, then run the full suite and (if UI changed) `npm run dev` in `packages/dashboard`.
4. Report to the user: what merged, test results, and any handoff caveats.

## Limits
- Max 3–4 concurrent workers (API rate limits, CPU when suites run in parallel).
- Workers have no network: no new dependencies unless pre-installed in `.venv`.
- Workers never run git; `dispatch.sh` commits their work on `agent/<name>`.
